# Kanban card gates

Hard stops before **edits** (governance, card body, product code). Read [agent-routing.mdc](agent-routing.mdc) and [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) § Classify quickly. Signatures: `kanban-prompt-ask-vs-agent`, `kanban-cursor-mode-gates`.

**Cursor mode:** infer Ask / Plan / Agent from session context; **stop** on mismatch for **`Plan @card`**
or **`Inquire @card`**. Full matrix: [reference.md § Cursor mode gates](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#cursor-mode-gates-plan--inquire--verbs).

## 1. Kanban card required (product work)

**Do not** edit application code or ship product fixes unless the user assigned a **kanban card** under
`.devtool/features/` **and** used an **agent verb** (§2).

| User prompt | Mode | Allowed |
| ----------- | ---- | ------- |
| Question, explain, audit | **Ask-only** | Read-only |
| Fix / implement / refactor **without** naming a card | **Ask-only** | Stop — kanban card required |
| Names a card but **review-only** verb (§2) | **Ask-only** | Read card + codebase; chat only |
| **`Plan @card`** / **`Inquire @card`** alone | **Plan** / **Ask** | Chat only — **no** product code; spawn **feature** / **agent** for implementation |

**No surgical / ad-hoc product implementation** without a card + agent verb.

## 2. Prompt verb gate (card named)

Classify the user message **before** editing any file. Case-insensitive; `@path` or
`.devtool/features/…` counts as naming a card.

| Intent | Example prompts | Cursor mode | Edits |
| ------ | --------------- | ----------- | ----- |
| **Review card** | `review @…`, `review foo-2026-06-25`, `Kanban: review …` | Any | Read + report in chat — **never** edit card |
| **Bare card attach** | `@.devtool/features/foo.md` only | Any | Summarize — no edits until agent verb |
| **Inquire** | `Inquire @card`, `Inquire …` | **Ask** | Chat research only — **no** card file edits |
| **Plan** | `Plan @card`, `Plan …` | **Plan** | Chat plan/roadmap only — **no** card file edits |
| **Update card** | `update …`, `update @card` | **Agent** | Card `.md` (+ scoped work per label) |
| **Plan approved** | `plan approved`, `approved`, `plan … approved` | **Agent** | **`plan`** card — write **Recommendation** |
| **Review + update** | `review and update …`, `review and implement …` | **Agent** | Rare — research + card write same turn |
| **Plan + update** | `plan and update …` | **Agent** | Rare — Plan exploration + **Recommendation** same turn |
| **Spawn from card** | `spawn cards from …`, `spawn follow-up` | **Agent** | New **todo** cards |
| **Implement card** | `implement …`, `work on …`, `continue …` | **Agent** | Full card lifecycle |
| **Card Done** | `Done`, `QA complete`, … | **Agent** | Move + Card Done — [reference § QA-complete](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#qa-complete--card-done-trigger-table); disambiguation gc9; Signature: `card-done-agent-move-qa-complete` |
| **Epic audit** | `epic complete`, `close epic {Name}`, … | **Agent** | gel0 anchor audit — [reference § Spawn, epics](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#spawn-epics-and-drift); **`### Epic summary`** |
| **Archive group batch** | `archive group {Name}`, `{epic} done archive`, … | **Agent** | gel3 batch — **`### Initiative summary`**; not on Card Done |
| **Single-card archive** | `archive @card`, `archive card {id}`, `archive {stem}` | **Agent** | gel5 — card in **`done/`** → `archived/` via `move_kanban_card.py`; move-only — no Card Done; not gel3 batch — Signature: `governance-single-card-archive` |
| **Legacy inquiry** | `Kanban: answer inquiry on …` | **Ask** then **Agent** | **Deprecated** — treat as **`Inquire`** (Ask, chat); user then **`update @inquiry-card`** (Agent) for **Response** — not same-turn card write |
| **No card / default** | anything else | Per §1 | Per §1 |

**Card-update allowlist:** edit kanban card markdown only when prompt includes `update …`,
`plan approved`, `approved`, `plan … approved`, or rare compounds above — not on bare `@path`,
`review …`, `Inquire …`, or `Plan …` alone.

**Upgrade:** if ask-only review finds work needed, tell the user to retry with `review and update`,
`update`, `plan approved`, `spawn`, or `implement`.

## 3. Frontmatter label required

Every kanban card **must** have a recognized type in frontmatter `labels` (inline JSON array).

| `labels` | Type | Card Done lessons |
| -------- | ---- | ----------------- |
| `["feature"]` | Feature | **Required** — [kanban-feature-cards.mdc](kanban-feature-cards.mdc) |
| `["bug"]` | Bug | **Required** — [kanban-bug-cards.mdc](kanban-bug-cards.mdc) |
| `["agent"]` | Agent | **Required** — [kanban-agent-cards.mdc](kanban-agent-cards.mdc) |
| `["inquiry"]` | Inquiry | **Not allowed** — [kanban-inquiry-cards.mdc](kanban-inquiry-cards.mdc) |
| `["plan"]` | Plan | **Not allowed** — [kanban-plan-cards.mdc](kanban-plan-cards.mdc) |
| `["commit-issue"]` | Commit-issue | **Required** — [kanban-commit-issue-cards.mdc](kanban-commit-issue-cards.mdc) |
| `["feedback"]` | Feedback | **Not allowed** — [kanban-feedback-cards.mdc](kanban-feedback-cards.mdc) |

**Invalid** — stop **all** work on that card: missing `labels`, `labels: []`, or unknown label.

**Active cards (feature/bug/agent/commit-issue):** agent completes **Product**, **Tests**, and **Docs**
before **Review**; **Tests → Verify (agent)** cites `scripts/pre-commit-pytest.sh` — draft **Tests →
Files** via `scripts/resolve_card_tests.py` (Signature: `precommit-pytest-scope-mismatch`,
`kanban-card-scope-schema`). Scoped `kanban-*-cards.mdc` hold detail.

## 4. Lessons learned scope

| Label | **Done** / **QA-complete** |
| ----- | -------------------------- |
| `feature`, `bug`, `agent`, `commit-issue` | Move + Card Done — lessons always; ff per [reference § Forward-feedback capture cadence](../skills/kanban-markdown/reference.md#forward-feedback-capture-cadence) |
| `inquiry`, `plan`, `feedback` | Move only — no lessons or parent-style ff |

